 "assembly": {
  "method": "CFRP sleeve wound on a ground 1:500 tapered steel mandrel (filament winding, wet T800S / high-Tg epoxy, Tg >= 190 C, post-cure 180 C), ID ground if needed; rotor magnet OD + end rings ground to the same 1:500 taper after bonding; rotor chilled to -150 C in LN2 vapour (no immersion: SmCo thermal shock), sleeve at 20 C pushed on axially with a servo-hydraulic press (force + stroke recorded) to the stroke that gives the interference; dry-film PTFE lubricant on the magnet OD",
  "taper": "1:500 on diameter",
  "interference_mm": 0.563,
  "press_stroke_mm": 281.5,
  "chill_shrink_mm": 0.179,
  "remaining_press_interference_mm": 0.384,
  "contact_pressure_20C_MPa": 94.4,
  "mu_assembly": 0.05,
  "F_press_warm_kN": 465,
  "F_press_chilled_kN": 317,
  "sleeve_axial_stress_at_push_end_MPa": 127.7,
  "layup": "88 % hoop (88-89 deg) + 12 % +/-15 deg helical (inner 0.4 mm + outer 0.4 mm) -> axial compressive strength of the laminate ~350 MPa",
  "note": "push on a split steel ring against the full sleeve end face; axial stress at the pushed end must stay < 0.5 x 350 MPa -> chilling + PTFE dry film are mandatory; final checks: OD growth vs. stroke, magnet / sleeve contact by ultrasonics, OD ground cylindrical 120 h6"
 },
 "decision": "CFRP (T800S-class, 7 mm, hoop-wound) sleeve with a 0.563 mm diametral interference: magnets stay in contact at the 108 % trip (cold) and the hot 120 % spin test, hoop stress 1018 MPa at 100 % hot (40 % UTS_eff) and 1060 MPa at the spin test (38 % UTS); non-conducting -> no sleeve eddy loss; light (220 m/s self-stress 76 MPa). Inconel 718 rejected: self-stress 396 MPa at 100 % / 570 MPa at 120 % leaves no margin for the magnet load (von Mises over Rp0.2 at the spin test for every thickness that fits) and a conducting sleeve adds 7200 W of eddy loss in the rotor."
}